WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.030
Two identical cars.

2
00:00:02.080 --> 00:00:06.150
One is speeding along a motorway
at thirty metres per second.

3
00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:08.910
The other is parked, perfectly still,

4
00:00:08.960 --> 00:00:11.870
on the edge of a cliff
forty metres high.

5
00:00:11.920 --> 00:00:15.030
The speeding car has
energy because it moves.

6
00:00:15.080 --> 00:00:18.410
The parked car has energy
because it is high up.

7
00:00:18.460 --> 00:00:20.630
Same car, same mass.

8
00:00:20.680 --> 00:00:22.970
Which one holds more energy?

9
00:00:23.020 --> 00:00:26.490
In this mission, you'll calculate
kinetic energy from mass and

10
00:00:26.540 --> 00:00:29.500
speed, and see what happens
when the speed doubles.

11
00:00:29.550 --> 00:00:33.230
You'll calculate gravitational
potential energy from mass and

12
00:00:33.280 --> 00:00:34.410
height.

13
00:00:34.460 --> 00:00:38.410
Your mission: decide which
car holds more energy.
